<!--BlockML Documentation — copy A02 pages into A03 and author semantic structure
  FQN: org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task.A03_AuthorPages-->
<task:A03_AuthorPages xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:task="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.task"
  xmlns:workflow="org.blockml.bml.transformer.workflow"
  xmlns:source="org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source"
  xmlns:type="org.blockml.bml.type">

  <baseType>
    workflow:InstructionTask
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A task that copies A02 pages into A03 and authors their semantic structure
  </is>
  <documentation>
    A03 authoring task: copy every A02 page into A03, link the copies in
    BmlDocSet_A03 and the A03 PageGroups, then enrich each page with the
    semantic scaffold that A04 will render.

    - **Copy** — identity (title, purpose, detailLevel, pageType, is) comes
      from the A02 skeleton; an existing A03 page is overwritten
    - **Deletion** — an A03 page that is not in A02 is deleted
    - **Links** — pages, groups, and see / source / Navigation targets may
      name only A03 Blocks or lib Blocks from authorativeSources; never a
      Block from another sector
    - **Semantics** — after the copy, author learningObjectives,
      readerOutcomes, scopes, exclusions, authoritativeSources, and content
      as a specification of what to show, not as finished rendered prose
    - **Template** — org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
      is the structural pattern only, not a domain-content source
    - **Sources** — authorativeSources is BlockMLSourceSet, the same set as
      A02_UpdatePageSkeletons
  </documentation>
  <properties>
    <instructions type="type:Text" override="true">
      <value>
        <![CDATA[
          Copy A02 pages into A03, register them on the A03 DocSet and
          PageGroups, then author the semantic structure that specifies what
          each page must show. Sector 3 writes specification, not the
          finished site. Sector 4 (A04_RenderingSector) renders prose,
          examples, and code from that specification.

          All domain content comes from this task's authorativeSources and
          from the A02 skeleton fields (title, purpose, detailLevel,
          pageType, is, documentation, see links). Do not read BmlDocSetPlan
          as the identity source. Do not invent pages that are not in
          BmlDocSet_A02.pages. Do not edit A02 pages, A02 PageGroups, or
          BmlDocSet_A02. Do not write Pages outside a03.

          Use org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
          only as a structural template (member shape, content roles,
          how sources bind to annotations). Do not copy its domain claims
          onto other pages. Existing A03 page content is never
          authoritative: discard it and regenerate; keep only the FQN /
          file path so the same Block is overwritten.

          1. Read the A02 pages
          Read org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.BmlDocSet_A02.
          Walk BmlDocSet_A02.pages in A02 order. For each listed A02
          DocPage, inspect is, isNot, documentation, references/see, title,
          purpose, detailLevel, and pageType. Those fields are the copy
          source. Also note BmlDocSet_A02.homePage and, on each A02
          PageGroup, pages and landingPage — those slots are remapped after
          the A03 pages exist.

          2. Open the authoritative sources
          Resolve this task's authorativeSources TypeSelectors (scan type
          for each selector on org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.source.BlockMLSourceSet).
          That set is the same whitelist as A02_UpdatePageSkeletons:
          org.blockml.bml.constraint.**, org.blockml.bml.core.**,
          org.blockml.bml.definition.**, org.blockml.bml.documentation.**,
          org.blockml.bml.exception.**, org.blockml.bml.group.**,
          org.blockml.bml.language.**, org.blockml.bml.mapping.**,
          org.blockml.bml.meta.**, org.blockml.bml.relation.**,
          org.blockml.bml.service.**, org.blockml.bml.status.**,
          org.blockml.bml.type.**, org.blockml.bml.unit.**,
          org.blockml.bml.validation.**.

          Those lib Blocks are the only non-A03 Blocks an A03 page may
          reference (see, authoritativeSources, annotation sources). Never
          link a Block from another sector (a01, a02, a04, or any later
          sector). Never keep an A02 page or PageGroup FQN on an A03 page.
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.lib.** (for example BlockMLSourceSet and
          lib rules) may also be referenced. Docgen types
          (org.blockml.bml.docgen.**) may appear as structural see-links
          (for example Navigation on an Index page), not as sector content.

          For each candidate source, inspect is, documentation, and
          references — do not guess from the FQN alone.

          3. Resolve A03 page FQNs
          The a03 subpackages data, page, and pagegroup
          (org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page,
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.pagegroup) are created
          by A03_CopyDocSet if they do not already exist. This task does
          not create those packages. Create descendant page packages
          (for example data.page.docs) when an A03 page FQN requires them.

          Page FQN =
          replace the prefix org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page
          with org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page
          (for example
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a02_structuring.data.page.docs.Intro
          → org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page.docs.Intro).

          Write only under this a03 page package tree, never a page package
          outside a03.

          4. Copy each A02 page into A03 (overwrite if present)
          For each A02 page, resolve the A03 FQN (step 3). If that A03 page
          already exists, keep only the FQN / file path and overwrite the
          file. If it does not exist, create it. Do not invent pages that
          are not in BmlDocSet_A02.pages.

          Example of the target path:
          packages/bmldocs/blocks/org/blockml/bml/bmldocs/a03_authoring/data/page/docs/Intro.bml

          Carry identity from the A02 skeleton:
          - use baseType org.blockml.bml.docgen.page.DocPage
          - use the A02 Block name as the Block name
          - set is from the A02 page
          - set isNot from the A02 page when the A02 page has isNot
          - override title, purpose, detailLevel, and pageType from A02
          - copy see links that point at lib Blocks allowed by step 2
            (typically org.blockml.bml.documentation.* Requires / SeeAlso)
          - drop every see link that points at another sector
          - omit docset

          5. Delete A03 pages that are not in A02
          List every DocPage under
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.page (including
          descendants). If its Block name / relative FQN after .data.page.
          is not among the remapped A02 pages from step 1, delete that A03
          page file and remove it from org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library.
          Do not delete pages outside a03. Do not delete
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.example.PageExample_A03
          — that Block is the structural template, not a DocSet page.

          6. Link the A03 pages in the DocSet and PageGroups
          Update org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.a03_authoring.data.BmlDocSet_A03
          when that DocSet exists. Put every A03 page written in this task
          into BmlDocSet_A03.pages (TypeReferenceEntity links, A02 order).
          Remove any pages entry that is not one of those A03 pages.
          Set BmlDocSet_A03.homePage from BmlDocSet_A02.homePage, remapped
          to the A03 counterpart. homePage, when set, must be one of the
          A03 pages in pages. Omit homePage when A02 has none. Never list
          an A02 page in pages or homePage.

          For each A03 PageGroup that exists, rebuild pages from the
          matching A02 PageGroup: for each A02 pages entry, append the
          A03 counterpart written in this task (A02 order); skip if that
          A03 page was not written. Remap landingPage the same way, or
          omit it when there is no A03 counterpart. parentGroup must stay
          an A03 PageGroup. If an existing group slot points outside a03,
          remove it. Do not create or delete PageGroups here —
          A03_CopyPageGroups owns group identity. If BmlDocSet_A03 or a
          group does not exist, skip that container.

          7. Bind sources and author the semantic specification
          For each A03 page, start from the A02 purpose, title, and see
          links. From the Blocks allowed by step 2, select the SSOT
          Blocks that actually cover that purpose. Those selected Blocks
          are the page's authoritative sources. Every content page must
          have at least one Requires see-link to a lib SSOT Block. If
          several match, Requires = primary SSOT; SeeAlso = supporting
          background. Do not attach a source that does not serve the
          purpose.

          Then enrich the page after the pattern of PageExample_A03.
          Inspect that example, then inspect the DocPage / ContentElement /
          semantic types. Each authored page must:

          - declare page-level authoritativeSources as an
            AuthorativeSourceSet whose includedTypes are the bound lib
            SSOT FQNs (not sector FQNs)
          - author learningObjectives, readerOutcomes, scopes, and
            exclusions as owned semantic instances (summary + optional
            authoritativeSources / reason), grounded in the bound sources
            and the A02 purpose — not copied from PageExample_A03
          - author content as an ordered semantic scaffold: Section
            (heading + purpose + nested content) and ContentElements
            (Paragraph, List, ListItem, CodeBlock, Navigation as needed)
          - on each ContentElement set purpose, message, role
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.role.*), detailLevel
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.level.*), and weight
            (org.blockml.bml.docgen.weight.*)
          - attach supportingPoints and exclusions on elements when they
            sharpen the claim; bind their authoritativeSources to lib
            Blocks from step 2
          - omit CodeBlock.code — A04 generates the listing from message,
            supportingPoints, exclusions, and authoritativeSources
          - omit finished reader-facing article prose, HTML, and filled
            example bodies; message states the claim to convey, purpose
            states why the element exists for the renderer
          - for pageType Index (for example TableOfContents): author a
            Navigation tree whose NavigationItem targets are A03 pages
            only (from the remapped A02 / A03 groups). Do not invent
            conceptual body on an Index page
          - NavigationItem.target and any in-page continuation link may
            name only A03 pages written by this task
          - never list an A02, A01, or A04 Block in see,
            authoritativeSources, annotation sources, or Navigation

          The result is a page that specifies exactly which ideas,
          sections, roles, and sources A04 must manifest — not the
          manifested page itself.

          8. Export A03 pages from the catalog
          Export each A03 page written here from
          org.blockml.bml.bmldocs.Library if it is not already in the
          catalog. Do not remove catalog entries of other sectors. Do not
          remove PageExample_A03 if it is catalogued.
        ]]>
      </value>
    </instructions>
  </properties>
  <aggregations>
    <authorativeSources override="true">
      <composition>
        <source:BlockMLSourceSet />
      </composition>
    </authorativeSources>
  </aggregations>
</task:A03_AuthorPages>
